#N canvas 40 40 2500 1620 12;
#X text 20 20 lp-step0 -- the Phase 6 Step 0 measurements \, items 82 to 87. NOT an Organelle patch and not Cut It code: it talks straight to the Launchpad through midiout and touches nothing else. Run it on the MAC with the Launchpad plugged in \, and keep the Pd console window visible -- that is where every reading appears., f 70;
#X text 20 130 EVERYTHING YOU CLICK IS IN THIS COLUMN \, top to bottom \, in the order you need it. The machinery is off to the right and needs nothing. NOTHING IS SENT AT LOAD except the output port \, deliberately: an automatic init fires before you have chosen the MIDI device \, which is exactly how the first version of this patch wasted a run., f 70;
#X text 20 280 1 -- MODE. This unit comes up in Programmer Mode already \, so the first click is a re-assert rather than a switch. Click LIVE at the end of the session., f 44;
#X msg 20 370 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 14 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 20 420 s \$0-byte;
#X text 480 370 PROGRAMMER MODE. Click once to prove the port works before trusting anything below., f 26;
#X msg 20 480 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 14 \, 0 \, 247;
#X obj 20 530 s \$0-byte;
#X text 480 480 LIVE MODE -- THE ESCAPE HATCH \, and the only way to reach the device's Setup menu. Leave it here when you finish., f 26;
#X text 20 610 2 -- COLOUR. Click one of these FIRST \, then a size below. These are palette indices \, not brightness., f 44;
#X msg 20 690 5;
#X msg 90 690 21;
#X msg 170 690 45;
#X msg 250 690 0;
#X obj 20 750 s \$0-colour;
#X text 340 690 5 red / 21 green / 45 blue / 0 off, f 26;
#X text 20 830 3 -- SIZE. One SysEx carrying this many colour specs \, indices counting from 10 upward., f 44;
#X msg 20 910 64;
#X msg 90 910 99;
#X msg 170 910 120;
#X obj 20 970 s \$0-size;
#X text 340 910 64 is the baseline that must work. 99 reaches index 108 \, so it covers the 8x8 grid AND the whole outer ring -- items 83 and 84 in one press. 120 is deliberately OVER the documented 106 limit \, and what matters is HOW it fails: the first hundred-odd lit and the rest dark means truncated \, everything dark means rejected., f 44;
#X text 20 1070 4 -- LAYOUT. Item 87. All three ids are GUESSES \, and finding the real ones is the measurement. After each \, come back to Programmer Mode and LOOK BEFORE CLEARING -- whether the colours survived is what says if the re-clear is optional., f 44;
#X msg 20 1200 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 0 \, 0 \, 247;
#X obj 20 1250 s \$0-byte;
#X text 480 1200 layout-select 0, f 26;
#X msg 20 1320 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 0 \, 4 \, 247;
#X obj 20 1370 s \$0-byte;
#X text 480 1320 layout-select 4, f 26;
#X msg 20 1440 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 0 \, 5 \, 247;
#X obj 20 1490 s \$0-byte;
#X text 480 1440 layout-select 5, f 26;
#X text 800 280 WHAT THE DEVICE SENDS BACK. Three prints \, and the console is the instrument here., f 60;
#X obj 800 380 notein;
#X obj 800 440 pack f f f;
#X obj 800 500 print NOTE-pitch-vel-ch;
#X text 800 550 Pads are NOTES \, r*10+c \, both digits 1 to 8 and ROW 1 AT THE BOTTOM -- so 11 is bottom-left and 88 is top-right. Already verified in position \; here only as a sanity check that input is arriving at all., f 44;
#X obj 800 700 ctlin;
#X obj 800 760 pack f f f;
#X obj 800 820 print CC-val-num-ch;
#X text 800 870 ITEM 82 IS THIS PRINT \, and it gates step 6. Press all 32 ring buttons and read the MIDDLE number. Documented: 91 to 98 across the top \, 99 the logo \, 89 79 69 59 49 39 29 19 down the right \, 80 70 60 50 40 30 20 10 down the left \, 101 to 108 along the bottom. If this unit disagrees \, the unit wins., f 44;
#X obj 800 1080 polytouchin;
#X obj 800 1140 pack f f f;
#X obj 800 1200 print AT-val-note-ch;
#X text 800 1250 ITEM 86. Hold one pad hard \, then two at once: TWO HELD PADS MUST REPORT INDEPENDENT VALUES. One shared value means the device is still in Channel Pressure -- go to Live Mode \, hold Setup \, press the third Track Select button \, choose Polyphonic Aftertouch., f 44;
#X text 1500 280 THE MACHINERY. Nothing over here needs clicking., f 60;
#X obj 1500 380 loadbang;
#X obj 1500 430 del 3000;
#X msg 1700 480 1;
#X obj 1500 540 r \$0-byte;
#X obj 1500 600 midiout;
#X text 1500 660 ONE midiout \, fed by a send \, so every byte in this patch leaves by one door and the port is set in one place -- the cold inlet at load \, which is u_init's proven pattern. If nothing lights \, suspect this port before suspecting the bytes., f 44;
#X text 1500 790 THE BATCH GENERATOR -- items 83 and 84 \, and the whole phase's mitigation. Header 240 0 32 41 2 14 3 \, then N times a type byte \, an index and a colour \, then 247. Type 0 is static palette. Indices count from 10 \, and the device ignores the ones that do not exist -- which is what u_init's existing clear loop already relies on., f 60;
#X obj 1500 920 r \$0-size;
#X obj 1500 950 t b f b b;
#X msg 1500 1020 247;
#X obj 1500 1080 s \$0-byte;
#X obj 1700 1020 until;
#X obj 1700 1080 f;
#X obj 1700 1140 t f f;
#X obj 1900 1200 + 1;
#X obj 1700 1200 + 10;
#X obj 1700 1260 t b f b;
#X obj 1700 1330 s \$0-byte;
#X obj 1980 1330 f 5;
#X obj 1980 1390 s \$0-byte;
#X msg 2220 1330 0;
#X obj 2220 1390 s \$0-byte;
#X obj 2200 1260 r \$0-colour;
